Design: We improve the ResNet18‐based pipeline by adding simple test‐time augmentation: for each image we extract deep features from both the original and a horizontally flipped version, average them to produce more robust representations, and then use these features for logistic regression. This adds minimal overhead but typically boosts generalization by reducing sensitivity to orientation. We then perform 5‐fold stratified cross‐validation with these TTA features, train the final model on all data, and update `predict()` to apply identical TTA during inference. Finally we report the mean CV AUROC and save `submission.csv`.
